04-010113:
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Pilates Soft Over Ball&lt;/strong&gt; is a soft, inflatable small ball used for pilates and musculoskeletal rehabilitation. It supports posture improvement, activates deep muscles, enhances balance, and increases body awareness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What is the Soft Over Ball?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This ball usually has a diameter of 20–30 cm, with a lightweight and soft structure. It is fully or partially inflatable, making it adaptable for various exercises. Its material is typically non-slip PVC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who is it recommended for?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Beginners&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Older adults&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Those requiring rehabilitation&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Advanced practitioners&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Instructors, physiotherapists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Usage possibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Strengthening the abdomen, back, thigh, and gluteal muscles&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Posture improvement&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Balance exercises while sitting or lying down&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Shoulder and hip mobilization&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Relaxation and stretching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why is size important?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The size of the ball (usually between 17–29 cm) determines how unstable or supportive it is. Selecting the correct size is important for comfort and effectiveness during exercises.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Larger ball: more stable, provides more support&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Smaller ball: more unstable, requires more muscle work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Summary&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Pilates Soft Over Ball&lt;/strong&gt; is a versatile tool that aids in muscle strengthening, balance development, and posture improvement. It is recommended for all levels, from beginners to advanced users, and suitable for both home and therapeutic use.&lt;/p&gt;

04-050101:
&lt;h2&gt;Hollow Massage Roller&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This massage roller is designed for experienced roller users ready for the “agonizingly pleasant” pain. Its material is firmer, and the textured surface targets knots and tense muscles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://shop.unas.hu/shop_ordered/21500/pic/Termekek/rehabilitation/Mambo-Max-Hollow-use.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Mambo-Max-Hollow-use.jpg&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Some pain during rolling is acceptable, but it must remain tolerable. The pain should subside within 30 minutes and must not cause irritation or lasting discomfort.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Common mistakes&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Rolling directly on the painful area
Take your time and start massaging the area around the painful spot before treating the problem area.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Treatment too fast.
If you roll the body part too quickly, the muscles won&#039;t have time to adjust to the compression and respond. Therefore, rolling too fast won’t resolve adhesions. Perform rolling with slow movements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Focusing too much on one point. Excessive and strong pressure can damage tissue or nerves. The essence of rolling is to gently roll the pressure over a particular muscle group.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

