– mineral salt baths (body, foot soak)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ingredients:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;NaCl 96–98%&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;additional minerals: Mg&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt;, Ca&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt;, iron, zinc, etc.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;

G5614:
&lt;p&gt;The StimVet 2000 is a muscle and pain relief electrostimulation device designed for treating small animals (cats, dogs) and horses.
In veterinary rehabilitation and physiotherapy, electric current is used for two primary purposes: reducing the sensation of pain and stimulating excitatory tissues (muscles).
The electricity promotes pain relief through membrane hyperpolarization based on the Gate control theory, as well as increased hyperemia and elevated levels of morphine-like mediators.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Device size and weight: 10 x 16 x 3.5 cm, 440 g&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Cat and dog treatment programs&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pain relief (TENS)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Endorphin TENS&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Conventional pain relief TENS&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Modulated TENS&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Post-surgical pain&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Fracture pain&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Osteoarthritis&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Cartilage degeneration (discopathy)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Spondylosis&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lumbosacral joint&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Wobbler syndrome (dogs only)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rehabilitation&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Post-ACL regeneration&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Muscle contracture (stiffness)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Prevention of muscle atrophy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Muscle strengthening&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Muscle strengthening for Wobbler syndrome (dogs only)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Microcurrent programs&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Osteogenesis (bone formation aid)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Wound healing support&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Cartilage formation stimulation&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Muscle strengthening (SPORT) (dogs only)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Maximum force&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Endurance strength&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Explosive strength&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Muscle relaxation&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Muscle &quot;cooling&quot; (calming)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Denervated muscle treatment&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Triangle 1-2-3&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Trapezius 1-2-3&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Quadrilateral 1-2-3&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Horse treatment programs&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pain relief (TENS)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Endorphin TENS&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Conventional pain relief TENS&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Post-surgical pain&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Fracture pain&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Osteoarthritis&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Cartilage degeneration (discopathy)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Spondylosis&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rehabilitation&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Post-ACL regeneration&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Muscle contracture (stiffness)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Prevention of muscle atrophy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Motor point probe&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Microcurrent programs&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Osteogenesis (bone formation aid)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Wound healing support&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Cartilage formation stimulation&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;

E-TRALNE:
&lt;p&gt;TensCare Neck Pain electrode is specifically designed for neck electrotherapy treatments. The self-adhesive electrode connects to medical-standard devices. It features a snap connector, and the package includes four adapters for use with 2mm pin connector devices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Instructions for Use&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preparation:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the skin is clean and dry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do not apply electrodes to damaged or numb skin areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Connection:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insert the lead connectors into the electrode’s snap sockets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure both connectors fit securely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Application:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn off the device before applying the electrodes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Place the electrodes on the painful area with the adhesive side against the skin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gently press the electrodes onto the skin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Removal:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grip the edge of the electrode and peel it off gently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avoid pulling on the lead wires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Storage:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After use, place the electrodes back on the plastic protective film.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Store them in the resealable bag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Tips &amp; Advice&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure electrodes are clean and sticky for optimal conductivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replace electrodes when they lose adhesiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrode gel may soften in warm temperatures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Warnings&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you experience an allergic reaction, discontinue use and consult a physician.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrodes are intended for single-user only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use only with stimulators compliant with EN 60601-1 and EN 60601-2-10 standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Electrode Placement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply to the back of the neck and shoulder area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://shop.unas.hu/shop_ordered/21500/pic/elektroterapia/Neckpain.png&quot; alt=&quot;Neck Pain electrode&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Storage Information&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrode life spans 12–20 uses, depending on skin condition and humidity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stored in original packaging, shelf life is 2 years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avoid extreme temperatures and low humidity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

G5948:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Magnum TotalBody 400 magnetic therapy mat is not a standalone device but an accessory connectable to Magnum magnetic therapy devices.&lt;/strong&gt; It only works when connected to magnetic therapy devices!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;The TotalBody 400 mat consists of four units measuring 44x70 each.&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;All of these are active, containing magnetic coils, with each having 4 coils. That&#039;s a total of 16 coils.&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;The mats can be attached to each other with Velcro.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://shop.unas.hu/shop_ordered/21500/pic/magnesterapia/Total-Body-400-foam-matrac-szekciok.png&quot; alt=&quot;Total-Body-400-foam-mat-sections.png&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended use:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Most magnetic therapy treatments recommend long, multi-hour sessions which are ideally done overnight during sleep.&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;For many people (e.g., those with fixed work schedules) who lack daytime availability for long treatments, the magnetic therapy mat allows treatment during sleep.&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;The mat also enables treatment for patients confined to bed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preparing, positioning, and getting ready for treatment with the Magnum TotalBody 400 mat&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;The mat sectors attach to each other with Velcro.&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Each sector contains 4 solenoids (magnetic coils), generating a magnetic field along the entire length.&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Place the mat on the bed’s lying surface and lie down on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Operating the Magnum TotalBody 400&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Connect the mat to the Magnum device.&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Select the appropriate program from the device menu and start it.&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li&gt;Sleep peacefully; the device automatically switches off after the treatment time ends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
